    "result": "## Summary\n\nI've successfully fixed all failing tests in the frai-core suite. Here's what was wrong and how I fixed it:\n\n### Issue 1: governance.test.js - \"flags schema violations with descriptive errors\"\n**Problem**: The test imports `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but it was only exported in the default export object.\n\n**Fix**: Added named exports for all governance functions and constants at the top of `/packages/frai-core/src/finetune/index.js`, keeping the default export for backward compatibility.\n\n### Issue 2: eval/index.test.js - \"runs default evaluations\"  \n**Problem**: The `toxicityMetric` function had an inconsistent signature compared to other metrics. When `runEvaluations` called it with `(outputs, references)`, the references array was being passed as the `bannedTerms` parameter instead of using the default, causing all content to be flagged as toxic.\n\n**Fix**: Updated `toxicityMetric` function signature to accept `(outputs, _references, bannedTerms = defaultBannedTerms)`, matching the pattern of other metrics while ignoring the references parameter.\n\n### Results\n\u2705 All 28 tests passing across 8 test files  \n\u2705 All public exports remain intact and working",
